  "conclusion": "Single-ring proves scheduler aggregation can halve up/down iouring batch count and reduce wait by roughly 50%, without increasing reads/bytes. However, token rate does not improve because single-ring also serializes H2D/copy work and loses the existing dual-stream overlap. The next source change must decouple disk read aggregation from H2D stream fanout.",
  "next_direction": "Implement a default-off read-aggregate/H2D-fanout path: aggregate up/down read jobs through one iouring submission batch, but enqueue H2D copies to separate CUDA streams or preserve current up/gate stream split after reads complete. Acceptance requires reads/bytes not increase, batch count lower, wait lower, TTFT within limit, and token rate above current generalized SOTA."
